{"id": "tea:sivananabodham:1", "source": "src:sivananabodham", "location": {"ref": "1", "section": "pramāṇa-iyal (proofs)"}, "paraphrase": "The world, spoken of as 'he, she and it', undergoes origination, maintenance and dissolution; therefore it has an agent. It resolves into Hara and, because of mala, comes forth again from him; hence the learned say that he who is its end is also its beginning.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "world-fate"], "terms": ["trm:pati", "trm:mala"], "concepts": ["cpt:pati-pasu-pasa", "cpt:five-acts-of-siva"], "disputes": ["dsp:isvara", "dsp:causation"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:sivananabodham:2", "source": "src:sivananabodham", "location": {"ref": "2", "section": "pramāṇa-iyal"}, "paraphrase": "The Lord is one with souls and yet other than them (like the soul with the body, the vowel with the consonants); by his command (āṇai, his power) he stands inseparably with them and makes them come and go through births according to their twofold deeds (iruviṉai).", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:iruvinai", "trm:arul"], "concepts": ["cpt:siddhanta-advaita", "cpt:grace-anugraha"], "disputes": ["dsp:souls-one-or-distinct"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:sivananabodham:3", "source": "src:sivananabodham", "location": {"ref": "3", "section": "pramāṇa-iyal"}, "paraphrase": "There is a soul within the body distinct from it: it denies that it is this or that ('not this'), it says 'my body', it knows through the five senses, it knows in dream, it does not experience in deep sleep, it is awakened, and it knows only when made to know.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "terms": ["trm:pasu"], "concepts": ["cpt:soul-as-sadasat"], "disputes": ["dsp:is-there-a-self"], "notes": "The list of the soul's marks is summarized from memory; the exact enumeration should be checked against the text.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:sivananabodham:4", "source": "src:sivananabodham", "location": {"ref": "4", "section": "lakṣaṇa-iyal (definitions)"}, "paraphrase": "The soul is not one of the inner organs (antaḥkaraṇa); bound by its innate mala it cannot know by itself, and it knows through the inner organs as a king through his ministers; it passes through the five states (avasthā).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "terms": ["trm:anava-mala", "trm:avastha"], "concepts": ["cpt:five-avasthas"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:sivananabodham:5", "source": "src:sivananabodham", "location": {"ref": "5", "section": "lakṣaṇa-iyal"}, "paraphrase": "The senses know their objects only through the soul yet do not know the soul; the soul likewise knows only through Śiva, who moves it as a magnet moves iron while himself remaining unchanged.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "ultimate"], "terms": ["trm:arul"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:sivananabodham:6", "source": "src:sivananabodham", "location": {"ref": "6", "section": "lakṣaṇa-iyal"}, "paraphrase": "What is known by the senses is changing and perishing (acat); what cannot be known at all would be non-existent; the Real (Śiva) is neither — it is known by the soul through grace, not as an object.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "apophatic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "terms": ["trm:cemporul"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:sivananabodham:7", "source": "src:sivananabodham", "location": {"ref": "7", "section": "cātaṉa-iyal (means)"}, "paraphrase": "Before the Real, the unreal does not appear; the unreal cannot know the Real; the soul, which knows both, is neither — it is sadasat (cat-acat), taking on the nature of whatever it is joined to.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "ultimate"], "terms": ["trm:sadasat"], "concepts": ["cpt:soul-as-sadasat"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:sivananabodham:8", "source": "src:sivananabodham", "location": {"ref": "8", "section": "cātaṉa-iyal"}, "paraphrase": "To the soul that has done penance in former lives, the Lord comes as the guru and teaches: 'You have lived among the five senses like a prince brought up among hunters'; the soul then leaves them, knows it is not other than the Lord, and reaches his feet.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "devotion"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:guru", "trm:arul"], "concepts": ["cpt:guru-as-siva", "cpt:saktipata"], "paths": ["pth:saiva-siddhanta-four-padas"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:sivananabodham:9", "source": "src:sivananabodham", "location": {"ref": "9", "section": "cātaṉa-iyal"}, "paraphrase": "Seeing Śiva in one's own soul with the eye of knowledge given by grace, knowing the senses' world as a mirage (pēyttēr), taking refuge in the Lord's shade, and meditating on the five letters as prescribed, the soul is purified.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "sound-language"], "terms": ["trm:pancaksara"], "concepts": ["cpt:pancaksara"], "practices": ["prc:pancaksara-japa", "prc:saiva-jnana"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:sivananabodham:10", "source": "src:sivananabodham", "location": {"ref": "10", "section": "payaṉ-iyal (fruit)"}, "paraphrase": "As the Lord is one with the soul, so the soul becoming one with him, acting only as his servant, is no longer touched by mala, māyā and the two deeds.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "devotion"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:iruvinai", "trm:mala"], "concepts": ["cpt:siddhanta-advaita"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:sivananabodham:11", "source": "src:sivananabodham", "location": {"ref": "11", "section": "payaṉ-iyal"}, "paraphrase": "As the soul makes the eye see and itself sees, so Śiva makes the soul know and himself knows; by unforgetting love the soul reaches his feet.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "consciousness-mind"], "terms": ["trm:anpu"], "concepts": ["cpt:siddhanta-advaita"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:sivananabodham:12", "source": "src:sivananabodham", "location": {"ref": "12", "section": "payaṉ-iyal"}, "paraphrase": "Having washed away the three malas that hide the Lord's feet, the freed soul should join the true devotees and worship their holy garb and the temple as the Lord himself.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "ritual"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["ethics", "practice"], "terms": ["trm:atiyar"], "practices": ["prc:mahesvara-puja"], "concepts": ["cpt:jivanmukti"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:sivajnanabodha:1", "source": "src:sivajnanabodha", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "The Sanskrit first verse argues from the world's threefold character and its three functions that it has a maker, into whom it is withdrawn and from whom it comes forth again.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "world-fate"], "cross_refs": ["tea:sivananabodham:1"], "notes": "Parallel of Civañāṉa Pōtam 1; wording not checked.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:sivananasiddhiyar:parapakkam", "source": "src:sivananasiddhiyar", "location": {"ref": "parapakkam"}, "paraphrase": "The opponents' section sets out in their own terms and then refutes the Lokāyata, the four Buddhist schools, the Jains, the Ājīvikas, the Mīmāṃsakas, the grammarians' word-Brahman, Māyāvāda Vedānta, Bhāskara's view, the Pāñcarātra, the Sāṃkhya and others, as a preparation for the Siddhānta.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["dispute"], "disputes": ["dsp:world-real-or-appearance", "dsp:is-there-a-self"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-circles-of-schools"], "notes": "Fourteen schools are traditionally counted; the list here is partial and moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:sivananasiddhiyar:cupakkam.1", "source": "src:sivananasiddhiyar", "location": {"ref": "cupakkam.1"}, "paraphrase": "The Lord performs the five acts — creation, maintenance, destruction, concealment and grace — not for himself but out of compassion, so that souls may exhaust their karma and ripen their mala; even destruction is rest for the souls.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "world-fate"], "concepts": ["cpt:five-acts-of-siva"], "terms": ["trm:pancakrtya"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference; exact verse not given.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:sivananasiddhiyar:cupakkam.2", "source": "src:sivananasiddhiyar", "location": {"ref": "cupakkam.2"}, "paraphrase": "God's non-duality with souls means not identity but inseparability: he is one with them, different from them and together with them, as the vowel is in the consonants; the Vedic sayings of oneness are to be understood so.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:siddhanta-advaita"], "disputes": ["dsp:liberation-identity-or-equality-with-siva", "dsp:souls-one-or-distinct"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:sivananasiddhiyar:cupakkam.8", "source": "src:sivananasiddhiyar", "location": {"ref": "cupakkam.8"}, "paraphrase": "When the two deeds come into balance and the soul's mala has ripened, Śiva's power descends (catti nipātam) in four grades — very mild, mild, intense and very intense — fitting the soul for caryā, kriyā, yoga or jñāna; Śiva then comes as the guru and initiates.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "teacher-transmission"], "terms": ["trm:iruvinaiyoppu", "trm:malaparipaka", "trm:saktipata"], "concepts": ["cpt:iruvinaiyoppu", "cpt:malaparipaka", "cpt:kinds-of-saktipata"], "paths": ["pth:saiva-siddhanta-four-padas"], "disputes": ["dsp:cause-of-saktipata"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference; the grade-to-path mapping is moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:sivananasiddhiyar:cupakkam.8/2", "source": "src:sivananasiddhiyar", "location": {"ref": "cupakkam.8"}, "paraphrase": "The guru initiates in seven ways — by look, touch, word, thought, instruction in the scriptures, yoga, and the fire rite (auttiri) — destroying the accumulated karma; the prārabdha that formed the body is exhausted by experience.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:diksa", "trm:prarabdha"], "concepts": ["cpt:kinds-of-diksa"], "practices": ["prc:diksa"], "disputes": ["dsp:does-diksa-liberate"], "notes": "The list of seven kinds is recalled at moderate-low confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:sivananasiddhiyar:cupakkam.8/3", "source": "src:sivananasiddhiyar", "location": {"ref": "cupakkam.8"}, "paraphrase": "Caryā, kriyā, yoga and jñāna are four steps; the first three give the lower liberations (sālokya, sāmīpya, sārūpya) and ripen the soul; only jñāna, given by the guru's grace, leads to union (sāyujya). Jñāna itself proceeds by hearing, reflection, clarity and abiding (kēṭṭal, cintittal, teḷital, niṭṭai).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["action", "ritual", "meditation", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:carya", "trm:kriya", "trm:sivayoga", "trm:sivajnana", "trm:salokya", "trm:samipya", "trm:sarupya", "trm:sayujya", "trm:nittai"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-padas", "cpt:four-kinds-of-mukti"], "practices": ["prc:saiva-carya", "prc:saiva-kriya", "prc:saiva-yoga", "prc:saiva-jnana"], "paths": ["pth:saiva-siddhanta-four-padas"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:sivananasiddhiyar:cupakkam.11", "source": "src:sivananasiddhiyar", "location": {"ref": "cupakkam.11"}, "paraphrase": "In liberation the soul does not become Śiva nor perish; it abides inseparable from him, enjoying his bliss, as the malas, which are eternal, lie powerless.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:siddhanta-advaita"], "disputes": ["dsp:liberation-identity-or-equality-with-siva", "dsp:mala-substance-or-ignorance"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:irupa-irupatu:1-20", "source": "src:irupa-irupatu", "location": {"ref": "1-20"}, "paraphrase": "In question and answer with his guru Meykaṇṭār, Aruṇanti asks how the soul, pure by nature, came to be bound, why mala clings to it, and how grace works; the answers teach that āṇava is beginningless and that only the guru's grace releases the soul.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "teacher-transmission"], "terms": ["trm:anava-mala"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:unmai-vilakkam:36", "source": "src:unmai-vilakkam", "location": {"ref": "36"}, "paraphrase": "The dance of the Lord is the five acts: creation from the drum, protection from the hand that grants fearlessness, destruction from the fire, concealment from the planted foot, and release (grace) from the raised foot.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["world-fate", "ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:dance-of-nataraja", "cpt:five-acts-of-siva"], "terms": ["trm:ananda-tandava", "trm:pancakrtya"], "notes": "Verse number moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:unmai-vilakkam:pancaksara-section", "source": "src:unmai-vilakkam", "location": {"ref": "pancaksara-section"}, "paraphrase": "In the five letters na-ma-śi-vā-ya, 'na' is concealment (tirōtam), 'ma' is mala, 'śi' is Śiva, 'vā' is his grace (aruḷ) and 'ya' is the soul; the soul standing between mala and Śiva should turn toward grace; placing 'śi' first (śivāya nama) is the subtle form.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "terms": ["trm:pancaksara"], "concepts": ["cpt:pancaksara"], "practices": ["prc:pancaksara-japa"], "notes": "Section-level reference; the letter correspondences are recalled with moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:unmai-vilakkam:tattva-section", "source": "src:unmai-vilakkam", "location": {"ref": "tattva-section"}, "paraphrase": "The body and world are made of thirty-six tattvas: twenty-four of the soul (ātma-tattva: the elements, subtle elements, organs and inner organs), seven of knowledge (vidyā-tattva: māyā, kalā, kāla, niyati, vidyā, rāga, puruṣa) and five of Śiva (śiva-tattva); the soul must know them as not itself.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:thirty-six-tattvas"], "terms": ["trm:tattva"], "notes": "Section-level reference.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:unmai-neri-vilakkam:1-6", "source": "src:unmai-neri-vilakkam", "location": {"ref": "1-6"}, "paraphrase": "The ten acts (tacakāriyam): seeing the form of the tattvas, seeing that they are insentient, purifying oneself of them; seeing the form of the soul, seeing the soul, purifying the soul; seeing the form of Śiva, seeing Śiva, union with Śiva (śiva-yoga) and enjoyment of Śiva (śiva-bhoga).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:tacakariyam"], "concepts": ["cpt:ten-karyas"], "paths": ["pth:saiva-siddhanta-ten-karyas"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:tiruvarutpayan:1.1", "source": "src:tiruvarutpayan", "location": {"ref": "1.1"}, "paraphrase": "As the vowel 'a' pervades all letters, the Lord, without equal, pervades everything as knowledge.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "original": {"text": "அகர உயிர்போல் அறிவாகி எங்கும் நிகரில் இறைநிற்கும் நிறைந்து", "script": "Tamil", "edition": "from memory; to be checked"}, "concepts": ["cpt:siddhanta-advaita"], "cross_refs": ["tea:tirukkural:1"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:tiruvarutpayan:ch.3", "source": "src:tiruvarutpayan", "location": {"ref": "ch.3"}, "paraphrase": "The chapter on the dark mala (iruḷ-mala-nilai): āṇava is one, beginningless and hides the soul's knowledge as darkness hides objects — but, unlike darkness, it hides itself as well; it is removed not by the soul's effort but by grace.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "consciousness-mind"], "terms": ["trm:anava-mala"], "obstacles": ["obs:anava-mala"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:tiruvarutpayan:ch.4", "source": "src:tiruvarutpayan", "location": {"ref": "ch.4"}, "paraphrase": "The chapter on grace (aruḷatu-nilai): grace is always present with the soul, as the sun's light is to the eye, yet the soul does not see it while covered by mala; grace is Śiva's own power.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:arul"], "concepts": ["cpt:grace-anugraha"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference; the sun image is recalled at moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:tiruvarutpayan:ch.5", "source": "src:tiruvarutpayan", "location": {"ref": "ch.5"}, "paraphrase": "The chapter on grace embodied (aruḷ-uru-nilai): as a deer is caught with a decoy deer, Śiva takes human form as the guru to catch souls who know only human forms.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:guru-as-siva"], "notes": "Chapter-level; the decoy image is recalled at moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:tiruvarutpayan:ch.9", "source": "src:tiruvarutpayan", "location": {"ref": "ch.9"}, "paraphrase": "The chapter on the five letters (aintheḻuttu-aruḷ-nilai): the right order of the five letters places grace between Śiva and the soul, and meditating them so leads the soul to Śiva.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["sound"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["sound-language", "practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:pancaksara"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:tiruvarutpayan:ch.10", "source": "src:tiruvarutpayan", "location": {"ref": "ch.10"}, "paraphrase": "The chapter on those who have attained (aṇaintōr taṉmai): the freed live without 'I' and 'mine', their acts are Śiva's acts, and they neither seek nor reject.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:jivanmukti"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:civappirakacam:1-100", "source": "src:civappirakacam", "location": {"ref": "1-100"}, "paraphrase": "The whole system in a hundred verses: the guru's lineage; the three padārthas; the soul's three states (kēvala, sakala, śuddha); the malas; the tattvas; grace, the guru and the means; and the bliss of release.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-avasthas-of-the-soul", "cpt:pati-pasu-pasa"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:cankarpa-nirakaranam:1-20", "source": "src:cankarpa-nirakaranam", "location": {"ref": "1-20"}, "paraphrase": "Umāpati refutes nine neighbouring views of soul, bonds and release — among them that the freed soul becomes equal to Śiva in every respect (Śivasamavāda), that the soul passes over into Śiva (Saṅkrāntavāda), that bonds remain like stone (Pāṣāṇavāda) — and upholds inseparable union in which the soul enjoys Śiva's bliss.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["dispute", "karma-liberation"], "disputes": ["dsp:liberation-identity-or-equality-with-siva"], "concepts": ["cpt:siddhanta-advaita"], "notes": "Locator is a placeholder range for the whole work; the characterizations of the nine views are low confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:tiruvuntiyar:1-45", "source": "src:tiruvuntiyar", "location": {"ref": "1-45"}, "paraphrase": "Grace alone brings the soul to Śiva; the guru's glance destroys the bonds; the one who knows by grace becomes one with Śiva without losing himself, and should remain in stillness.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:grace-anugraha"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:tirukkalirruppatiyar:1-100", "source": "src:tirukkalirruppatiyar", "location": {"ref": "1-100"}, "paraphrase": "Expanding the Tiruvuntiyār, it teaches the dissolution of the sense of 'I' in grace, the guru as Śiva, and the conduct of the jīvanmukta who acts without attachment.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:jivanmukti"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:kotikkavi:1-4", "source": "src:kotikkavi", "location": {"ref": "1-4"}, "paraphrase": "Four verses on the meaning of raising Śiva's flag: the soul's bonds are cut and grace is proclaimed; tradition says the stuck festival flag at Chidambaram rose as they were sung.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "tea:civanana-mapatiyam:sutra.2", "source": "src:civanana-mapatiyam", "location": {"ref": "sutra.2"}, "paraphrase": "Civañāṉa Muṉivar explains 'advaita' in the Civañāṉa Pōtam as 'non-separateness' (ananya), not numerical identity, and argues against the Māyāvādin reading of the Upaniṣadic identity sayings.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:siddhanta-advaita"], "disputes": ["dsp:world-real-or-appearance", "dsp:liberation-identity-or-equality-with-siva"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
